  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving livelihoods of Mexican families through community projects that include diaspora investment.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Instituto de Investigacin y Prctica Social y Cultural A.C. (IIPSOCULTA) will engage families in the Mexican states of Guerrero Mexico Puebla and Tlaxcala to improve livelihoods through the implementation of grassroots development projects that include diaspora investment. The project includes community-led action plans and financing for economic and cultural initiatives through diaspora investment in grassroots development. The grant includes assistance to strengthen IIPSOCULTA&apos;s organizational capacity. The grant will benefit 200 men and women directly and more than 500 family members indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
